# Force LF line endings on text files that run inside Linux containers
# (exploit.sh, prepare_app.sh, verify_files/*, etc.). Without this, Windows
# contributors with the default `core.autocrlf=true` get CRLF on checkout,
# which breaks bash inside the Linux exploit container with cryptic errors
# like `$'\r': command not found` and `cannot open '/path\r/file.py\r'`.
#
# Linux/macOS contributors are not affected — git treats LF as native and
# `text eol=lf` is a no-op there.
#
# Scope: every file extension below is something we expect to execute (or be
# imported into something that executes) inside a Linux container or on a
# Linux-side adb shell. Project-internal docs (.md) intentionally omitted —
# they're read by editors that handle either ending.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
